&title{The Wildfire}

&part#p1{I.}{The Gathering}

&chapter#p1c1{1.}{Smoke on the ridge}

The fire began at dawn. It spread across the ridge before anyone woke. By noon the whole valley was gone.

&chapter#p1c2{2.}{Ash and after}

She walked the burned line at dusk. &anchor#origin{where it all begins} The ground was still warm under her boots.

&anchor#lookback{a still moment}

They spoke of the smoke for years. The fire &anchor#firemark{} had a shape people remembered. Smith & Sons rebuilt the mill that autumn, and the R&D team studied the burn scars.

&part#p2{II.}{The Return}

&chapter#p2c1{1.}{New York, later}

A &chapter of accidents befell them on the road north. See &reference#origin{the opening} for how it started.

&chapter#p2c2{2.}{Threads} &anchor#thread{tie-off}

The letters came in a bundle. She read them out of order.

